### 6. Spillover Token Ratio (>20%)

**Purpose:** Monitors the economic efficiency of your setup. Fires when more than 20% of your total token throughput is being handled by the expensive Pay-As-You-Go shared pool instead of your pre-paid Dedicated pool.

* **Alert Name:** `Unified | PT vs Spillover Token Ratio > 20% | Gemini-2.5-Pro`
* **Condition:** `> 0.20`
* **PromQL:**

```promql
(
  sum by (resource_container, model_user_id) (
    rate(aiplatform_googleapis_com:publisher_online_serving_consumed_token_throughput{
      request_type="spillover", 
      model_user_id="gemini-2.5-pro"
    }[15m])
  )
  /
  sum by (resource_container, model_user_id) (
    rate(aiplatform_googleapis_com:publisher_online_serving_consumed_token_throughput{
      request_type="dedicated", 
      model_user_id="gemini-2.5-pro"
    }[15m])
  )
) > 0.20

```

* **Documentation Template:**

```markdown
# 💸 Cost Alert: High Spillover Traffic
**Project ID:** `${resource.labels.project_id}`
**Model:** `${metric.labels.model_user_id}`

**Details:** More than 20% of the token volume in `${resource.labels.project_id}` is spilling over into standard billing. Our Provisioned Throughput (PT) is undersized for current traffic.

**Playbook:**
1. Notify the FinOps/Billing team.
2. Evaluate if the GSU capacity assigned to `${resource.labels.project_id}` needs to be increased.
3. Check for inefficient prompt designs causing massive token consumption.

```

